# Cursor rules — spectacles-dimensional-os (monorepo)

This repository composes **`ARModule`** into DimOS blueprints and ships a
Specs Lens client and a WebXR host. It is **not a fork of DimOS** — import
the installed `dimos` package and wire via `autoconnect`.

## Names (DimOS-shaped)

Same pattern as `RelocalizationModule` / `dimos.mapping.relocalization` /
`unitree_go2_relocalization`:

| Role | Name |
|------|------|
| Class | `ARModule` in `dimos/ar/module.py` |
| Import | `dimos.ar` |
| Blueprint | `unitree_go2_ar` (`dimos run unitree-go2-ar`) |
| Wire peer | `server` — `time_sync.ts_client` / `time_sync.ts_server`, `state.server` |

Do **not** call it a bridge, an AR package, or `ar_go2`. Prose uses **`ARModule`**.
The WebSocket accept loop is a collaborator (`websocket/server.py`), not the class.
The Lens composition root is **`DimOSSpecsClient`**. Wearable UX lives under
`DimOSSpecsClient/presentation/` and `utilities/`. The WebXR composition root
is **`DimOSWebXRClient`**. Portable ClientCore lives under `DimOSARClient/`
(no `core/` folder).


## Chat — correct imprecise terms

When the user uses a technical term that does not match the protocol, API, or
abstraction layer under discussion, correct it in the reply before continuing.
Give the canonical term for that context. If a related term is also acceptable
at that layer, say so. Do not silently adopt the incorrect word.

## Layout

```text
spectacles-dimensional-os/
├── README.md                    # whole-project overview, setup, doc map
├── assets/                      # README gifs, demo media (NOT Lens Studio Assets/)
│   └── markers/                 # printable AprilTags + generate_marker.py
├── dimos-ar/                    # ARModule
│   ├── dimos/ar/module.py       # ARModule — DimOS In/Out surface
│   ├── dimos/ar/blueprints.py   # unitree_go2_ar
│   ├── PROTOCOL.md              # JSON WebSocket contract (cross-repo)
│   └── tests colocated under dimos/ar/
├── clients/
│   ├── core/                    # empty until ClientCore ships as .lspkg
│   ├── specs/                   # Specs client (Lens Studio project)
│   │   ├── spectacles-dimensional-os.esproj   # open THIS file (never from repo root)
│   │   └── Assets/Scripts/
│   │       ├── DimOSARClient/           # portable ClientCore (no core/)
│   │       └── DimOSSpecsClient/        # composition root + Specs host
│   └── webxr/                   # WebXR host
│       └── src/DimOSWebXRClient.ts  # composition root
└── launcher/                    # CLI scripts + web UI for setup/start
    ├── Start Launcher.command   # Finder double-click entry (http://127.0.0.1:8790)
    ├── scripts/                 # setup.sh, start.sh, start-launcher.sh, run-ci.sh, …
    └── app/                     # FastAPI launcher
```

| Component | Location | Notes |
|-----------|----------|-------|
| ARModule | `dimos-ar/dimos/ar/` | Platform-agnostic — no Specs logic |
| Blueprint | `dimos-ar/dimos/ar/blueprints.py` | `unitree_go2_ar` |
| Contract | `dimos-ar/PROTOCOL.md` | JSON WebSocket API |
| ClientCore | `clients/specs/Assets/Scripts/DimOSARClient/` | Headset-agnostic TypeScript in the Specs project until it ships as `.lspkg`. `clients/core/` is empty (`.gitkeep`). |
| Specs client | `clients/specs/` | Lens Studio project. Entry is `DimOSSpecsClient`. |
| WebXR host | `clients/webxr/` | Vite / XR Blocks. Entry is `DimOSWebXRClient`. |

The package publishes `dimos.ar*`. ClientCore production source is
`clients/specs/Assets/Scripts/DimOSARClient/` until the later `.lspkg` split.
`clients/core/` stays empty. Do not duplicate it.

## How we build dimos-ar

`dimos-ar/` is learning-first. Optimise for the human's comprehension, not for
throughput.

- **Subsystem groups.** Work proceeds in coherent groups (packaging, DimOS module,
  WebSocket layer, …). Within a group, finish one file at a time unless explicitly
  asked otherwise.
- **Explain before writing.** For each file, first state what it does, why it
  needs to exist, which DimOS API it touches (concrete path, line range when it
  matters), and which alternatives were rejected and why. Then pause.
- **Walk through after writing.** Explain the finished code and name the Python
  features it uses — dataclasses, protocols, context managers, async
  generators, descriptors. Assume the language itself is being learned.
- **Python ↔ TypeScript.** When explaining a Python-specific concept, give the
  TypeScript equivalent in one short clause, and vice versa. Same idea, two
  spellings — e.g. asyncio event loop ↔ JS/TS event loop; `Protocol` ↔
  `interface`; `async`/`await` ↔ `Promise`.
- **Match DimOS comment density.** Template files:
  `dimos/mapping/relocalization/module.py` and
  `dimos/robot/unitree/go2/blueprints/smart/unitree_go2.py`. No module-level
  essays, no class docstrings that restate the class, no section banners
  (`# --- … ---` — DimOS forbids them in `dimos/codebase_checks/test_no_sections.py`),
  no per-field comments that repeat the next line. A comment stays only when
  the code looks wrong or the constraint is invisible (surprising WHY, TODOs,
  end-of-line notes on config examples). Explanations go in chat.
- **Ask, do not assume.** When a real design fork appears mid-implementation,
  stop and ask in plain language with enough context to decide. Give at least
  two options, a recommendation, and the reason for it.
- **Prefer DimOS over new code.** Before writing anything, check whether DimOS
  already provides it, and say what you found either way.
- **Cite DimOS.** Any claim about DimOS behaviour needs a file path.

## Where to read first

| Area | Read |
|------|------|
| Whole project | `README.md` |
| WebSocket message schema | `dimos-ar/PROTOCOL.md` |
| Clients | `README.md` System Design + `CONTRIBUTING.md` |
| Spectacles / Lens Studio | [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](CONTRIBUTING.md) |
| Contributing | `CONTRIBUTING.md` |

## Planning

When fixing a bug, investigate and identify the root cause before writing a
plan. Plans must state the found issue and proposed solution up front, then list
implementation steps only. Do not create "investigation plans."

Plans are standalone documents: write only the final design and actionable
steps. Do not include Q&A history, rejected alternatives, migration tables from
earlier drafts, or "we decided against X" notes from prior plan iterations.

A plan is a singular piece, not a conversation or changelog of how it was
created. When revising or updating a plan file, rewrite it as the current plan
— do not refer to the previous version ("the plan had five blocking design
problems…", "previously we…", "this revision fixes…"). Readers should not need
the old draft to understand the new one.

## ARModule — systems design

When working in `dimos-ar/`, follow these constraints:

1. **One owner per concern** — each runtime concern has a single owning class; other
   code delegates rather than duplicating lifecycle or mutation logic.
2. **One source of truth** — do not mirror mutable state in two places; merge at encode
   time or read through the owner.
3. **Consistent, descriptive naming** — one concept, one name; prefer clarity over brevity.
4. **Explicit failures over silent fallbacks** — when a required value, configuration,
   or input is missing or invalid, raise or throw; do not substitute a hardcoded default
   that masks the problem. Use a fallback only when there is a deliberate, documented
   reason (e.g. backward-compatible wire defaults).

## State & lifecycle authoring

When adding lifecycle, wire handlers, coordinators, or presentation logic:

- **One concept, one name** — canonical type once; no parallel enums for the same flow.
- **Session + inputs + derive** — store event-sourced facts; rebuild inputs each read; never store derived UX state.
- **Derive; do not mirror** — one derivation function; wire owns execution truth.
- **Wire effects only** — reducer emits sends; controller owns presentation/teardown.
- **Presentation from state** — coupled UI from derived flags, not policy structs or duplicate bools.

## Non-negotiable facts

- **Never edit DimOS source.** Import from the installed `dimos` package. Upstream
  changes are filed as separate PRs.
- `dimos-ar/dimos/ar/` stays platform-agnostic. Portable TypeScript lives in
  `clients/specs/Assets/Scripts/DimOSARClient/` until it ships as an `.lspkg` (no Specs
  or Lens APIs in that tree). Specs-specific code lives in `clients/specs/`
  under `DimOSSpecsClient/`. The Specs composition root is `DimOSSpecsClient`.
  The WebXR composition root is `DimOSWebXRClient`. Do not call either
  `SpectaclesHost`. `clients/core/` is empty until the `.lspkg` split. WebXR
  imports ClientCore; it does not copy it.
- **Never edit** a second copy of ClientCore. There is no generated mirror and
  no `clients/specs/scripts/sync-client-core.mjs`.
- **Open Lens Studio from `clients/specs/spectacles-dimensional-os.esproj`**, not the repo
  root — opening at root creates stray `Cache/`, `Packages/`, etc.
- The cross-repo contract is `dimos-ar/PROTOCOL.md`. When the protocol
  changes, update the Python protocol and the client protocol module in the same change:
  - `dimos-ar/dimos/ar/websocket/protocol.py`
  - `dimos-ar/PROTOCOL.md`
  - `clients/specs/Assets/Scripts/DimOSARClient/websocket/protocol.ts`
- The ARModule worker must never block; WebSocket runs on a daemon thread.
- Blueprints are `unitree_go2_ar` and `unitree_go2_ar_agentic` (`dimos-ar/dimos/ar/blueprints.py`).
- Port **8787** is ARModule's WebSocket.
- Tests for `dimos.ar` must run from the DimOS `.venv`.
- For Lens Studio verification, do **not** run `CompileWithLogs` by default.
  Use normal compile checks first, and only run compile-with-logs when there is
  an actual compile/runtime error that needs investigation.
- Do **not** write or edit `clients/specs/Assets/Scene.scene` (or other `.scene`
  files) directly. Use the **`user-lens-studio` MCP tools** for scene-object
  investigation and manipulation. If the MCP cannot express a change, ask the
  user — do not patch scene files by hand.

## Pre-commit CI (agent commits)

Before any git commit, run `./launcher/scripts/run-ci.sh` from the repo root and fix failures
until it passes.

**Agents:** `run-ci.sh` must run **outside the Cursor sandbox** (`required_permissions: ["all"]`
or a normal terminal). Sandboxed runs fail when DimOS tries to write logs under
`~/.local/state/dimos/logs/`.

## Dev quick reference

```bash
# Local CI (matches GitHub Actions — run before committing)
# Must NOT run inside the Cursor agent sandbox — needs write access outside the repo
# (DimOS logs under ~/.local/state/dimos/logs/). Use a normal terminal or all perms.
./launcher/scripts/run-ci.sh

# Install + start ARModule (from repo root)
./launcher/scripts/setup.sh
./launcher/scripts/start.sh              # ws://0.0.0.0:8787
./launcher/scripts/start-launcher.sh     # web UI wrapper (http://127.0.0.1:8790)

# Tests
cd dimos-ar && /path/to/dimos/.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest
cd clients/specs/Tests && npm test   # ClientCore + Specs presentation tests; CI job client-specs-tests
cd clients/webxr && npm test         # WebXR host tests; CI job client-webxr-tests
```
